WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:16,670
Is there any harm in taking anti-dose enzyme therapy to my protocol? I've

00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:27,310
been reading your information on Dr. Gonzales. So Dr. Nicholas Gonzales was one of my teachers.

00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:38,430
He was a great guy. I liked him a lot and he was a protege. Dr. William Kelly. Well he took a lot

00:00:38,430 --> 00:00:46,670
information from Dr. William Kelly and he wrote several books on Dr. William Kelly. And he believed

00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:54,830
highly in high dose enzyme therapy. So he developed a product with allergy research that's called

00:00:54,830 --> 00:01:05,950
pancreas pork and it's using pork enzymes. Very high dose. And the theory was that very high dose

00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:11,150
enzymes take it on an empty stomach or relatively empty stomach. You'd absorb them.

00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:18,670
No, typically you take enzymes to help digest your food but this is taking enzymes in excess

00:01:18,670 --> 00:01:24,030
that then you'd absorb these enzymes and these enzymes would work in your body. They can help

00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:30,510
clean up, you know, clean up waste in your body but the real purpose with somebody with cancer would

00:01:30,750 --> 00:01:36,510
be to help break down the waste layer that's around the cancer so that any other therapy can

00:01:36,510 --> 00:01:45,230
attack the cancer. So is there any danger in taking using high dose enzyme therapy for someone?

00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:53,630
No, I don't think in general. No, I don't think there is a danger for anybody using high dose enzyme

00:01:53,710 --> 00:02:01,790
therapy. Is there downsides to high dose enzyme therapy? Well, just about a pill that you have to

00:02:01,790 --> 00:02:08,510
swallow depending on when high dose you're going. Dr. Gonzales used to have people take upwards of 75

00:02:08,510 --> 00:02:14,830
in the morning and 75 in the evening. But you don't have to go that high of a dose to still get some

00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:23,230
benefits of relative high dose therapy. But I don't see any negatives to doing any high dose enzyme

00:02:23,230 --> 00:02:29,230
therapy. You could make a giant argument. I think I have a video out there somewhere I talked

00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:36,670
about this a couple years ago, some research that came out that studied the different CT scans and

00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:46,030
MRIs of the general populace that they came to a working prognosis that people have it enlarged

00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:53,470
a pancreas. It was a study on why is pancreatic cancer rates going up. And they said that

00:02:54,030 --> 00:03:00,670
study showed that there that people in general have a much larger pancreas than the previous

00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:10,910
generations. And the theory was is that we're eating more chemicals in our foods that our

00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:18,510
denatured enzymes in the gut and therefore our pancreas is forced to enlarge to make more enzymes

00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:29,550
and there were having a relative decrease in enzyme utility and functionality. And therefore that's

00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:35,070
partly of what it can be causing disease and partly what can be leading to inflammation in the

00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:43,550
pancreas and therefore dysfunction and eventually cancer. So I don't know how much that theory has been

00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:49,710
proven but it does make sense from a working hypothesis that we do put a lot of stress on our pancreas

00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:59,230
and I have thought often about why functional medicine doctors from many years ago have recommended

00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:04,990
using pancreatic enzymes and have had success with not with cancer patients which is the general

